// expect: refuse E_ResumeOfNever
// `-> !` is the never type: an op that declares it never returns to its
// performer, so `!` is quantified per PERFORM and every consumer meets its
// own fresh variable. An arm that resumes such an op hands a value of one
// type to a performer that may stand at any type, so no resume of it is
// sound whatever it hands back. On boot 4228ff71 this compiled clean and ran
// to 4: the `!` was an effect parameter, the install fixed it at Int, and
// the op the declaration says never returns returned.
effect Stop {
  halt(code: Int) -> !
}

handler keep_going {
  halt(c) => resume(3),
}

fn f() = halt(3) + 1

fn main() -> Int = f() ~> keep_going
